    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0251" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/>

                <head>(M. 4558.)<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. W. Macalister to Board of
                        Trade</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >National Steamship Company</hi>, (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >limited</hi>,)<lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps">Drury
                            Buildings</hi>, 21 <hi rendition="#small-caps">Water
                                Street</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Liverpool</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 23, 1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of the 12th
                    instant respecting fog-signals at sea, and inclosing a proposal for the
                    consideration of the captains and officers in this company’s service, I have the
                    pleasure of inclosing a written report by several of our captains and officers
                    now in port, from which you will see that, for the most part, your proposal is
                    approved of, while one portion only of the plan is condemned. I may add, that I
                    quite agree with them in their remarks.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. B. MACALISTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General
                        Manager</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Assistant Secretary</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marine Department, Board of Trade</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
